    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0c456a5a-a250-55c4-854d-8251a2985944",
      ":question/problem": "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=- 2 x^{2} - 8 x - 10$ whose tangent has a slope of $-3.$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- 2 x^{2} - 8 x - 10.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f^{\\prime}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime}(x) &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(- 2 x^{2} - 8 x - 10\\right) \\\\\n&= (-2)\\cdot 2\\cdot x + (-8)\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= - 4 x - 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f^{\\prime}(x)=-3$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- 4 x - 8 &= -3 \\\\\n- 4 x &= 5 \\\\\nx &= - \\frac{5}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-3$ at the point where $x=- \\frac{5}{4}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
