      ":question/problem": "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=x^{2} - 6 x - 4$ whose tangent has a slope of $-5.$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=x^{2} - 6 x - 4.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f^{\\prime}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime}(x) &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2} - 6 x - 4\\right) \\\\\n&= (1)\\cdot 2\\cdot x + (-6)\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 2 x - 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f^{\\prime}(x)=-5$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 x - 6 &= -5 \\\\\n2 x &= 1 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-5$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$",
