      ":question/problem": "Find the **positive** $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=8 x^{3} - 60 x^{2} - 155 x - 5$ whose tangent has a slope of $-11.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=8 x^{3} - 60 x^{2} - 155 x - 5.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f^{\\prime}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime}(x) &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(8 x^{3} - 60 x^{2} - 155 x - 5\\right) \\\\\n&= (8)\\cdot 3\\cdot x^{2} + (-60)\\cdot 2\\cdot x + (-155)\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 24 x^{2} - 120 x - 155\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f^{\\prime}(x)=-11$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n24 x^{2} - 120 x - 155 &= -11 \\\\\n24 x^{2} - 120 x - 144 &= 0 \\\\\n24 \\left(x - 6\\right) \\left(x + 1\\right) &= 0 \\\\\nx &= -1,\\,6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x>0$, the required coordinate is $x=6.$",
